# Kaggle credentials for the Path A driver (run_kaggle.sh).
# Copy this to `.env` at the REPO ROOT (/home/ahmad/adaptishield/.env) and fill
# in your values. `.env` is git-ignored — never commit real credentials.
#
# ── Which credentials? ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The installed kaggle CLI is 1.7.4.5, which authenticates with a
# USERNAME + KEY pair (HTTP basic auth). The newer "API Tokens (Recommended)"
# access tokens need kaggle CLI >= 1.8.0 (not on PyPI) or kagglehub >= 0.4.1,
# so they do NOT work with this CLI. Use the LEGACY key instead:
#
#   kaggle.com → Settings → API → (legacy section, below "API Tokens")
#     → Create New Token  → downloads kaggle.json = {"username":..., "key":...}
#   Put those two values below. (Or just drop that kaggle.json in ~/.kaggle/ —
#   run_kaggle.sh falls back to it if these vars are unset.)

KAGGLE_USERNAME=your_kaggle_username
KAGGLE_KEY=your_legacy_api_key
